      "content": "#### Email\n\nTo: Orion Trip Desk\nFrom: Marco Lane\n\nI booked May 5. Your leaflet says heavy rain could strand us beyond the bridge. I prefer postponement to an improvised crossing. This plea is urgent because I must arrange leave. When is the decision made, and can my booking transfer? I can ask my employer about a different date, but need notice rather than a change on arrival."
    },
    {
      "title": "Reply",
      "type": "triple",
      "content": "#### Reply\n\nDear Mr. Lane,\n\nThe guide reviews conditions at 6 p.m. on May 4. If unsafe, we postpone to May 12 and transfer your booking unless you request a refund. We will not try an unplanned crossing. Members receive a message after the review. Keep both dates in mind when arranging leave. The same equipment requirements apply to the alternative date."
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": 195,
      "text": "When will the decision be made?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "At the postponed outing"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "The evening before the original outing"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "Noon on May 12"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "A week after May 5"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "B",
      "explanation": "May 4 at six is the evening before May 5. The other times are incorrect.",
      "speech": []
    },
    {
      "id": 196,
      "text": "What happens by default if the crossing is unsafe?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "A second payment"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "Automatic transfer to May 12"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "Cancellation without alternatives"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "An unmarked crossing"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "B",
      "explanation": "Transfer is automatic unless a refund is requested. The reply rejects improvised crossing and mentions no extra fee.",
      "speech": []
    },
    {
      "id": 197,
      "text": "How does the reply reflect the charter?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "It guarantees no accidents"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "It avoids unnecessary risk"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "It encourages dares"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "It allows ignoring the guide"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "B",
      "explanation": "The refusal of an improvised crossing follows the safety principle. Neither a total guarantee nor risky behavior is promised.",
      "speech": []
    }
  ]
}

